From 5cc3dfce7f0b40cdfc3c982d3c534b2267230693 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: dwc: add Samsung Exynos 9820 GEN2 PCIe host driver

DesignWare based host driver for the GEN2 PCIe controller of the
Exynos 9820, which carries the BCM4375 Wi-Fi chip on the Galaxy S10
family, with its binding.

System sleep (sleep_off): the link is powered off over suspend-to-RAM
(2, default), always (1) or never (0); with 3 the Wi-Fi chip supply is
kept on over suspend-to-RAM so that its firmware survives. If the link
does not come back after a sleep, the chip is power-cycled once
(resume_repower_ms).

While the link stays up in suspend-to-idle, the chip's wake pins
(wlan-host-wake-gpios, wake-gpios) are armed as wakeup interrupts: the
chip sits in D3 and raises them when it needs the host.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
---
 .../bindings/pci/samsung,exynos9820-pcie.yaml | 121 +++
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Kconfig            |  14 +
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/Makefile           |   1 +
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-exynos9820.c  | 947 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 1083 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pci/samsung,exynos9820-pcie.yaml
